## Vercel Speed Insights Installation

Successfully installed and configured Vercel Speed Insights for the ModaPella frontend project.

### Changes Made:

**1. Package Installation:**
- Added `@vercel/speed-insights` version ^2.1.0 to dependencies
- Updated package-lock.json with the new package and its dependencies

**2. Code Integration:**
- **Modified:** `frontend/src/App.jsx`
  - Added import: `import { SpeedInsights } from '@vercel/speed-insights/react';`
  - Added `<SpeedInsights />` component to the App component's render tree
  - Placed the component at the root level within the CompareProvider context to ensure it loads on all pages

### Implementation Details:

The implementation follows the official Vercel documentation for React/Vite projects:
- Used the React-specific import path: `@vercel/speed-insights/react`
- Positioned the component at the application root to track all page views
- The component is lightweight and non-blocking, so it won't affect page load performance

### Framework Context:

- **Project Type:** Vite + React
- **Package Manager:** npm
- **Installation Method:** Followed the official Vercel Speed Insights quickstart guide (retrieved on 2026-11-15)

### Verification:

✅ Build completed successfully (`npm run build`)
✅ No linting errors (no linter configured in project)
✅ All dependencies properly installed and locked

### Next Steps:

Once deployed to Vercel, Speed Insights will automatically start collecting Web Vitals metrics including:
- First Contentful Paint (FCP)
- Largest Contentful Paint (LCP)
- Cumulative Layout Shift (CLS)
- First Input Delay (FID)
- Time to First Byte (TTFB)

Metrics can be viewed in the Vercel dashboard under the Speed Insights tab after users visit the deployed application.
